## std/state — the State<S> algebraic effect.
##
## Operation Piezoelectric Effects, Phase 2, Milestone P2.a.
##
## `State` is a stateful-cell effect: callers inside a `with State(v) do ... end`
## block can `get()` the current value and `set(new)` to replace it. Nested
## `with State(...)` blocks get their own independent slot — writes inside
## the inner block do not leak to the outer. This is the Koka / Xie-Leijen
## 2020 "evidence-passing" compilation strategy: each handle install pushes
## a per-install slot onto `@__qz_effect_stack_state_slots`, and the
## default handler reads/writes `slots[current_install_idx]`.
##
## Usage:
##
##   import std/state
##
##   def main(): Int
##     with State(0) do ->
##       set(get() + 1)
##       set(get() + 1)
##       return get()    # → 2
##     end
##   end
##
##   def main(): Int
##     with State(1) do ->
##       with State(2) do ->
##         return get()  # → 2 (inner slot)
##       end + get()     # → 2 + 1 = 3
##     end
##   end
##
## Type-parameter note: `State<S>` parses but `<S>` is erased at runtime —
## every value is i64-sized. For `State<Point>` / `State<String>` / etc.,
## the slot holds a boxed pointer encoded as i64 (standard Quartz existential
## type model). P2.a ships Int-only; boxed types work transparently because
## all pointers are i64-sized.
##
## Handler override: user `with State { get: my_get, set: my_set } do ... end`
## is supported via the H-delegate per-op install mechanism. Custom handlers
## receive the same `(op, argc, argv)` ABI as other effects; they can read
## the current slot via `__qz_effect_state_get()` / `__qz_effect_state_set(v)`
## if they want to cooperate with the evidence-slot machinery.

effect State
  def get(): Int
  def set(value: Int): Int
end
